WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.620
Hey there, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, Episode 62, it's June 5th, 2026.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.100
Let's break down today's coolest AI news so anyone can understand it.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:10.880
Let's go.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.680
So imagine you have a friend who keeps forgetting the details you told them yesterday.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.540
That is exactly the problem open AI just fixed with a new memory system for chat GPT.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.980
The system now tracks important details automatically instead of waiting for you to remind

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.120
it every single time.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:34.560
Think of it like a notebook that writes itself while you talk, highlighting the useful parts without you lifting a pen.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:42.280
Open AI also doubled the amount of memory available, so longer projects stay organized across many conversations.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.080
This matters because most people use AI for homework, stories, or plans that stretch over several days.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:54.260
When the AI forgets what you shared before, it feels like starting from scratch every morning.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:01:00.260
With better memory, it can build on your earlier ideas and give suggestions that actually fit your style.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:06.400
For students that could mean an AI remembering your writing habits and helping improve them across assignments.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.400
For creators, it could track themes you like in art or videos without you repeating them.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.560
The rollout started today for chat GPT Plus and pro users in the US.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:23.960
To try it, open the chat GPT app on your phone, make sure it is updated, and start a conversation about something you care about.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.000
Ask it to remember details like your favorite subjects or a project you are working on.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.480
Then check back tomorrow to see what it recalls on its own.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:38.000
Okay, now for my favorite part of the show, The Deep Dive, where we look under the hood.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:44.260
You know how when you are texting a friend your phone remembers the last few messages so the conversation makes sense.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:52.140
Now picture the AI keeping a running notebook of everything important you have set across many chats, not just the last few lines.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:59.980
It looks for patterns like this person always asks about science homework on weeknights or they are building a story about dragons.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:05.020
Then it uses that notebook to make future answers fit what it already knows about you.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.640
The system does not store every single word forever.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:15.900
It picks out the useful parts, the same way you might highlight key sentences in your notes instead of copying the whole textbook.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.860
And that is basically how the new memory feature works, not so mysterious, right?

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:32.320
Next up, cool stuff and try this. Open AI shared the story of one of their models finding a counter example to a famous math problem unsolved since the 1940s.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:39.960
Researchers worked with the AI to explore the problem step by step, showing how humans and models can team up on real discoveries.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:46.100
This proves AI can help push the boundaries of math and science, not just answer homework questions.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:54.000
If you love puzzles or want to see how future scientists might work, listen to the full conversation on the open AI podcast.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:03:02.580
Search for the episode titled How a Reasoning Model Cracked an 80-year-old conjecture on Spotify, Apple Podcasts, or YouTube.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:10.360
A team in Egypt just released Horus Lens, 1.0, their first text-to-image model made locally.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:17.660
It is part of a bigger effort to grow AI tools in the region and shows that cool AI work is happening all over the world.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:24.400
The model focuses on generating images from descriptions and early examples look promising for creative projects.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:32.780
If you enjoy making art or experimenting with visuals, check out the announcement and sample images shared on Reddit in the artificial community.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.720
Time for quick bits, the rapid fire stories you do not want to miss.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:44.120
A passenger discovered that the music and Uber driver was blasting came entirely from Suno, an AI music tool.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:52.840
The driver had no idea and still loved the songs after finding out, which shows how quickly AI creative tools are blending into everyday life.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:59.500
Several leading universities in South Korea are now covering the paid version of ChatGPT for their students.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:06.060
This highlights how access to better AI tools could affect learning opportunities depending on where you study.

